description:
Add proper lifecycle management for HikariDataSource pools.

Implementation:
1. createPool(String targetUrl, Properties info, Map<String,String> params) method
2. pools.computeIfAbsent() for thread-safe pool creation
3. Shutdown hook for graceful pool cleanup on JVM exit
4. Optional: closePool(String targetUrl) for explicit pool shutdown
5. Handle username/password from Properties

Shutdown hook:
```java
static {
    Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(new Thread(() -> {
        pools.values().forEach(HikariDataSource::close);
    }));
}
```

Files: src/main/java/org/pjdbc/drivers/HikariPoolDriver.java

Depends on: PJDBC-h03 (configuration must be implemented)

The existing maxCacheRows limit protects against queries returning many rows, but not against queries returning few rows with large values (BLOBs, CLOBs, large TEXT fields).

## Problem

An attacker could bypass maxCacheRows by crafting queries that select large binary/text columns:
- 100 rows × 10 MB BLOB = 1 GB memory (passes 10,000 row limit)
- 1,000 rows × 1 MB TEXT = 1 GB memory (passes 10,000 row limit)

## Proposed Solution

Add `maxCacheBytes` config parameter (default: 10MB, 0=unlimited):

```java
// In CacheConfig
private final long maxCacheBytes;  // default: 10485760 (10MB)

// In CachedResultSet construction
long estimatedBytes = 0;
while (rs.next()) {
    if (maxRows > 0 && rows.size() >= maxRows) { exceeded = true; break; }

    Object[] row = readRow(rs);
    estimatedBytes += estimateRowSize(row);

    if (maxBytes > 0 && estimatedBytes >= maxBytes) { exceeded = true; break; }

    rows.add(row);
}
```

## Size Estimation

Simple estimator for common types:
```java
private static long estimateSize(Object val) {
    if (val == null) return 0;
    if (val instanceof String s) return s.length() * 2L;  // UTF-16
    if (val instanceof byte[] b) return b.length;
    if (val instanceof BigDecimal bd) return 48 + bd.toString().length();
    if (val instanceof Timestamp) return 24;
    if (val instanceof Date) return 16;
    // primitives (Integer, Long, Double, etc.)
    return 16;
}
```

## Affected Components

Same as maxCacheRows:
- CachingDriver
- MemcachedCachingDriver  
- RedisCachingDriver
- HazelcastCachingDriver
- SafeResultSetSerializer

## Usage

```
jdbc:cache:...?maxCacheRows=10000&maxCacheBytes=10485760
```

